 /* ============================================================
-   §startup-animations-v4 — re-add subtle but visible animations
-   to the loading screen per user feedback. Replaces the deleted
-   watermark + orbit grid with:
-   1. A faint floating-glow "aurora" — three slowly drifting radial
-      gradients in the brand color. Barely visible but adds depth.
-   2. A pulsing accent ring around the central brand mark — visible
-      enough to read as "the app is loading" without being noisy.
-   3. A slow horizontal "scan line" sweeping top-to-bottom — 6s cycle,
-      reads as a boot-time activity indicator.
-   All animations use the GPU-friendly opacity+transform only so
-   the WebView2 surface stays at 60fps even on low-end machines.
+   §startup-final-v5 — calm, deliberate loading screen.
+   The user explicitly disliked the rotating square "orbits",
+   the big RVL watermark, and the randomly moving dots.
+   This block keeps ONLY three subtle effects:
+   1. A single horizontal scanline sweeping top-to-bottom every 7s.
+      Barely visible (opacity 0.35) but reads as "loading activity".
+   2. A gentle "breathing" glow around the central RVL brand mark.
+      The pulse is slow (3s) and dim — never distracting.
+   3. The progress bar keeps its indeterminate fill, with a soft glow.
+   No watermarks, no rotating shapes, no particle dots.
    ============================================================ */
 
